Market-competitive salary

Do you get energized by creative and conceptual thinking? Do you perform well under pressure? Do you find it a challenge to bring together the technical and creative aspects? Then this is the role for you!

**What we are looking for:**
----------------------------

* A completed technical HBO (higher vocational education) degree, preferably in mechanical engineering, mechatronics, or a similar technical field;
* Several years of relevant work experience in mechanical design within machine building, preferably with packaging machines and automation robots;
* In-depth knowledge of 3D CAD software (e.g., SolidWorks, SolidEdge, or Inventor) and PDM/PLM applications;
* Experience with strength calculations and dynamic analyses is a plus;
* Knowledge of pneumatics, drives, and materials;
* Familiarity with standards and guidelines within machine building (e.g., CE markings);
* Strong analytical skills and problem-solving abilities;
* Experience with project-based work and multidisciplinary collaboration;
* Proficiency in Dutch and English;
* Experience with AutoCAD is a plus.

**Why choose Madern?**
----------------------

* A challenging and responsible position within a leading machine manufacturer;
* We work on innovative and complex projects within the packaging sector;
* A competitive salary;
* 27 holidays and 13 advanced annual leave days;
* Company laptop and mobile phone;
* 1 to 2 fixed home office days;
* Excellent training and development opportunities;
* Various informal activities and a Friday afternoon drink.

**Your benefits with us:**
--------------------------

### **Holidays**

27 holidays, 13 advanced annual leave days

### **Dynamic environment**

Challenging role in a vibrant setting.

### **Competitive salary**

In line with CAO metaal en techniek.

### **Activities**

Informal events and Friday drinks.

### **Education**

Opportunities for growth and development.

### **Hybrid working**

You can work both at the office and from home.

### **Laptop + mobile phone**

You will get your own company laptop and smartphone.

**About your role as a Senior Mechanical Engineer**
---------------------------------------------------

As a senior mechanical engineer, you are technically responsible for designing, developing, and improving innovative mechanical systems and machines within the packaging sector. You combine in-depth technical expertise with practical experience to create high-quality, efficient, and reliable machines that meet customer and market requirements. In this role, you work directly with the project engineer and are part of a multidisciplinary engineering team. You also collaborate closely with other disciplines such as hardware, PLC, and robotics engineering. You make a key contribution to complex projects, from the concept phase to commissioning, and support the resolution of technical challenges.

**Your responsibilities as a Senior Mechanical Engineer**
---------------------------------------------------------

* You design the mechanical systems and components for our machine solutions and develop them according to customer requirements;
* Prepare technical drawings, specifications, and concepts based on customer needs and project requirements;
* Select materials and components for optimal performance and durability;
* Create and review drawings and calculations related to the mechanical specifications at all stages of the project;
* Contribute to the continuous improvement of existing machines and processes;
* Identify trends and innovations within mechanical engineering and apply them to new designs;
* Contribute to the standardization of designs and components where possible;
* Identify technical bottlenecks during the engineering process and resolve them;
* Act as a mechanical expert within a multidisciplinary team;
* Monitor quality and cost control during the design phase;
* Support the in-house testing phase as well as the installation and commissioning phase at the customer site;
* Act as a key user for PDM and ensure that the PDM environment functions optimally for end users;
* Provide technical support in the procurement process;
* Assist the service department with after-sales activities.

